---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy"
  pageDescription="Privacy Policy for Thor Draper Jr's personal website and operator's notebook."
  currentPath="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="shell-container">
    <header class="post-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="post-heading">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="post-meta-row">
        <span>Last updated August 28, 2026</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="prose panel">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Thor Draper Jr. handles information connected to
        <a href="https://thordraperjr.com">thordraperjr.com</a>, including this website and
        applications or integrations operated for the site owner.
      </p>

      <h2>Information this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a static publication site. It does not provide visitor accounts, contact
        forms, comments, advertising profiles, or newsletter registration. I do not intentionally
        collect names, email addresses, profile data, or other personal information through the
        website itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        The hosting and delivery services used to make the site available may process limited
        technical information such as an IP address, browser details, request time, and requested
        URL in server or security logs. Those services control their own processing under their
        respective policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party resources and links</h2>
      <p>
        The site loads fonts from Google Fonts. A request for those fonts may be received by
        Google and is governed by Google's policies. The site also links to external services,
        including LinkedIn, GitHub, and email. Following an external link takes you to that
        service's website and privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>LinkedIn integration</h2>
      <p>
        I am developing an optional, approval-gated integration that can help prepare and publish
        content to my own LinkedIn profile through LinkedIn's official API. The integration is
        not a website form and does not collect information from visitors to this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        If I authorize that integration, LinkedIn may provide the application with information
        needed to authenticate my account and perform the approved action. Credentials and access
        tokens are stored outside this website and are not placed in blog content, repositories,
        or prompts. The integration will not publish generated content without my review and
        explicit approval of the exact text.
      </p>

      <h2>How information is used</h2>
      <p>
        Information available through normal hosting or security logs is used to deliver the site,
        protect it, diagnose failures, and understand operational issues. I do not sell personal
        information collected through this site, and I do not use visitor information to train an
        AI system.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Hosting and delivery providers may retain technical logs according to their own retention
        practices. Email correspondence is retained only as long as reasonably necessary to
        respond, maintain records, or meet legal obligations. LinkedIn data, if the separate
        integration is authorized, is limited to what is needed for that integration and handled
        according to LinkedIn's API terms and applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can avoid sending information by not contacting me through email or using external
        links. You may request information about personal data I directly control by contacting me
        at <a href="mailto:thordraper2@outlook.com">thordraper2@outlook.com</a>. Depending on your
        location, you may have additional rights under applicable privacy law.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        I may update this policy when the site or its integrations change. The revised policy will
        be posted at this URL with a new “Last updated” date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:thordraper2@outlook.com">thordraper2@outlook.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
